    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nFor Sale by DNG Online Auction TO REGISTER FOR OUR ONLINE AUCTION on the 3rd December 2026 at 3pm.Visit www.dngauctions.ieChoose/ Search for your property of interest, click log in & register to bid and follow the necessary steps.Bidder security required prior to auction date in order to successfully bid on the day.DNG Martin O'Connor Land Sales are delighted to offer for sale by DNG Online Auction this attractive parcel of grazing land at Rusheeny, Oughterard, Co. Galway.The property comprises Plot 4, shown hatched in magenta, forming part of a proposed subdivision of File Plan 80 of Folio GY4010F and extending to approximately 0.94 Ha (2.31 acres).Triangular in configuration, the lands enjoy good frontage onto a local country road and are currently in grazing use. The boundaries comprise a combination of traditional stone walls and wire fencing.The road frontage and manageable size of the parcel make it an attractive addition to an existing holding, while there may also be potential for a site, subject to obtaining the necessary planning permission and all relevant consents.This is a useful and well-positioned parcel of land in the scenic Rusheeny area, within easy reach of Oughterard Village.\n\nPlease note this property will be offered by online auction (unless sold prior). Vendors may decide to accept pre-auction bids so please register your interest with us to avoid disappointment. The successful bidder is required to pay the balance of 10% deposit and contracts are signed immediately on acceptance of a bid.Directions: From Oughterard village proceed along Main Street towards Clifden passing the Garda Station on your left. Just before the Bridge turn left at McNamaras Shop & the Beauty House salon it will be signposted Costelloe and Shannapheasteen. Drive out this road past the Oughterard Motors and take the next right turn onto the Rusheeny Road. Driving for about half a mile turn left a stone built shed with a green roof. Drive to dwelling with Eircode H91WYA3 and turn right Lot 4 is along this road on the left hand side with a DNG Martin O'Connor sign."
      },
      {
